[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mIs this app used by more than one person? "Users get notified when tasks change" usually implies someone else made the
[0;2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mchange.[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mMulti-user / shared tasks[39m
     [38;5;246mSeveral people see and edit the same tasks. This is what makes notifications meaningful — but it requires accounts,
[39m     [38;5;246mauth, a server, and shared persistence. Biggest scope, and the task app becomes a real backend project.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Single user, just me
     [38;5;246mOne person, one browser. Then 'someone changed a task' can't happen — notifications collapses to self-reminders: [39m
     [38;5;246mdue dates, overdue items, recurring tasks. Much smaller, no server or auth needed.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Single user, multiple devices
     [38;5;246mJust you, but synced across phone/laptop. Needs a server and sync, but no multi-account auth. Notifications cover [39m
     [38;5;246mdue dates plus 'changed on your other device'.[39m
